  "packageSHA256": "8448da040044e86623605a5ba533677d89465d581dfa7d11dc0da1e6f12e38ea",
  "helperSHA256": "882df284617255332dcd157c745fc8c5ca016a8815058292e2841646d470c8f9",
  "scope": "Exact installed Release in mimo-vm, saved real proxy, Rule/Global/Direct, real route events, foreign DNS owner, engine crash, ordinary-user connections and physical-interface captures. No physical sleep/unlock or simultaneous-login claim.",
  "finding": "After engine restart, holdGateUnderLock accepted the startup blocking parent because it contained power-guard and matched the newly written guard.expected. The supervisor retained its old installed-policy cache, skipped child/parent installation, and pointed an unreachable permission gate at the probe policy. Both lookups failed while traffic stayed blocked. Changing mode invalidated the cache and recovered.",
  "resolution": "Warm parent reuse now requires the permission anchor too; startup/damaged parents force full blocking fallback, invalidate the cached installation and install the real probe parent."
}
